{"t": 1794113084.782646, "kind": "call", "tool": "slack_post_message", "args": {"channel_id": "C07INCID003", "text": ":rotating_light: *AG-7731 PaymentGatewayErrors (checkout)* \u2014 root cause identified\n\n*Symptom:* Gateway 4xx rate ~38% for service=checkout since 07:41 UTC.\n*Cause:* The payment gateway switched to API version 2026-11 (\"strict amounts\"). It now requires `amount` as an integer in minor units (cents); checkout was still sending decimal euros, e.g. `{\"amount\": 12.34, \"currency\": \"EUR\"}` -> `400 invalid_amount: amount must be an integer in minor units (cents), got 12.34`.\n*Fix:* Updated `checkout/gateway.py` `charge_payload()` to convert EUR to integer cents with half-up rounding (12.34 -> 1234). Sanity-checked 0.01/0.1/1.005/5/12.34/19.99.\n*Next:* Deploy checkout, then confirm gateway 4xx rate returns to baseline and AG-7731 resolves. No other services observed sending decimal amounts."}, "ok": true}
